  "headline": "Police Search Kupang Regent Official Residence in Rape Case Probe",
  "seoTitle": "Kupang Regent Rape Investigation Update",
  "metaDescription": "Police searched the official residence of Kupang Regent Yosef Lede and seized evidence as part of an ongoing investigation into sexual assault allegations.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Law enforcement officials searched the Kupang Regent's residence, collecting items including a mattress and pillows as evidence.",
    "The NTT Regional Police have scheduled an examination of Regent Yosef Lede for next week following approval from the Ministry of Home Affairs.",
    "Police authorities have dismissed public speculation regarding a potential settlement, confirming that the criminal investigation is actively proceeding."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The NTT Regional Police are currently conducting an investigation into allegations of sexual assault involving the Kupang Regent, Yosef Lede, and a university student. As part of the ongoing inquiry, authorities have executed search warrants at the Regent's official residence, resulting in the seizure of five distinct pieces of evidence for forensic analysis. Additionally, police have conducted searches at the residence of a woman identified as EK in connection with the case. While some reports circulated rumors of a potential resolution outside of the legal process, the Indonesian National Police have officially denied these claims, asserting that the investigation remains active. The NTT Police have confirmed that formal questioning of the Regent is slated to occur next week, following the receipt of necessary authorizations from the Ministry of Home Affairs. The Criminal Investigation Agency (Bareskrim Polri) continues to provide assistance to the NTT Police throughout the proceedings.",
